&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;About the Role&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Corporate Sales Manager — Brazil to lead a high-performing team of Account Executives. As a HubSpot Sales Leader for our Brazil Corporate Account Executive team, you will execute our world-class sales methodology, hire exceptional talent, deliver sales quota each month, uncover strategies to coach and develop your team, and build a sales environment and culture we can be proud of.&lt;br&gt;The ideal candidate brings strong process rigor, a data-driven mindset, and a genuine passion for coaching and developing bilingual sales&amp;nbsp; talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;What are the responsibilities of a Corporate Sales Manager?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will need to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage a sales team to meet monthly goals: activity metrics, forecasted opportunities, territory plans and revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build confidence &amp;amp; trust with direct reports as well as provide developmental feedback for continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach team members to develop their professional sales skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold team members accountable of their performance and KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate well with other sales managers, directors &amp;amp; executives to aid the growth of the business as well as cross-functional teams across the organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise &amp;amp; conduct training on skills improvement, inbound sales, product &amp;amp; marketing topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sales skills &amp;amp; ability to teach sourcing and sales strategies to new team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain headcount via recruiting, selecting and training new Corporate Account Executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain professional and technical knowledge of inbound marketing and the HubSpot platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand your country market(s) and build and execute plans to grow them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate HubSpot core values and leadership traits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand leadership training styles and apply to interactions with direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;What are the role requirements?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience managing a quota-carrying sales team required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in English and Portuguese&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in Spanish is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing sales teams selling for Brasil.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams with consultative sales processes with upmarket companies, including managing complex deals with multiple stakeholders and developing business cases, proof of concepts, pilots and executive briefings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior coaching skills - ability to observe, evaluate &amp;amp; use various techniques to improve results and coach team members on HubSpot’s sales methodologies from prospecting to closing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail oriented and the ability to manage multiple objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytic skills to identify trends and gaps in activities and results in order to drive changes in team behaviors and build growth plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work cross functionally to drive business results through collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong individual &amp;amp; team motivation skills, with high self awareness and good interpersonal and EQ skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal responsibility to hit monthly team goal &amp;amp; positive attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is open to candidates that are&lt;strong&gt; based in Saõ Paulo&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
